                <pb facs="0638" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6531/462: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-05-11T12:00:00+01:00">May 11, 1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        May 11—7:22 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. Department’s instruction No. 466, April 11, 1939. Officials of the Ministry
                    of Foreign Trade and Exchange state categorically that the global quotas are now
                    inclusive of special agreements between Italy and other countries and that no
                    quotas exist outside of the global allotments.</p>
                <p>Note based on the Department’s instruction was delivered on April 25.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
